  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eswatini - Civil Unrest 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In December 2020, the Prime Minister of Eswatini died and that position has been vacant until today (30 June 2021). In January 2021, the country also lost two Cabinet Ministers to COVID-19, and they are also not replaced, leaving a huge leadership vacuum in the Executive arm of Government. 
Some members of Parliament started the calling for democracy in the country, something which stimulated youth to submit petitions in the different constituencies (where MPs are elected), with lists of issues which Government should address. Government issued a statement banning the submission of the petitions. The statements from government were not well received by the masses and they continued with the submission of petitions on the 26 June 2021, resulting in an altercation with police who were stopping the people.&#xa0; People responded by resorting to the protest. 
Since then protest have been sporadic, with targeted arson attacks have increase significantly.</narrative>
  </description>
